    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d87de684_9cd9b0ae",
        "filename": "board/servo_micro/board.c",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 447,
      "author": {
        "id": 1291807
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-08-02T22:07:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Which macros exactly?  Can you give an example using them for this?\n\nI didn\u0027t find any examples of macros being used for the \"mask\" arg to gpio_set_alternate_function().\n\nNote that GPIO_MASTER_I2C_SCL and GPIO_MASTER_I2C_SDA are 28 and 29, respectively.  They\u0027re not the bitmask values needed here.",
      "parentUuid": "bc2dce79_50415d53",
      "revId": "bf3d7d392472c74198367681671c0330c5985697",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "195c9438_00d64b50",
        "filename": "board/servo_micro/board.c",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 447,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000104
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-08-02T23:10:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You can do this in a slightly cleaner fashion like so:\nhttps://cs.corp.google.com/chromeos_public/src/platform/ec/board/servo_v4/usb_pd_config.h?l\u003d166\n\n\t\t\t/* USB_DUT_CC1_TX_DATA: PB14 is SPI2 MISO */\n\t\t\tconst struct gpio_info *g \u003d gpio_list +\n\t\t\t\tGPIO_USB_DUT_CC1_TX_DATA;\n\t\t\tgpio_set_alternate_function(g-\u003eport, g-\u003emask, 0);",
      "parentUuid": "d87de684_9cd9b0ae",
      "revId": "bf3d7d392472c74198367681671c0330c5985697",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f3ea3dff_2c182f99",
        "filename": "board/servo_micro/board.c",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 447,
      "author": {
        "id": 1129199
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-08-03T02:25:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Please do this:\n\nboard/servo_micro/gpio.inc:\nALTERNATE(PIN_MASK(B, 0x0300), 1, MODULE_SOMETHING, 0) /* XYZZ: PB08/PB09 - Description */\n\nHere:\n\ngpio_config_module(MODULE_SOMETHING, 1);\n\nThen disable when you are done:\n\ngpio_config_module(MODULE_SOMETHING, 1);",
      "parentUuid": "195c9438_00d64b50",
      "revId": "bf3d7d392472c74198367681671c0330c5985697",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e7a2dce3_c69a6b1d",
        "filename": "board/servo_micro/board.c",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 450,
      "author": {
        "id": 1129199
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-08-02T02:14:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why not use these macros?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 450,
        "startChar": 6,
        "endLine": 450,
        "endChar": 25
      },
      "revId": "bf3d7d392472c74198367681671c0330c5985697",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e34031cd_e51b5f0b",
        "filename": "board/servo_micro/board.c",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 450,
      "author": {
        "id": 1291807
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-08-02T22:07:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Those macro names are from STM\u0027s libraries.  AFAICT they don\u0027t exist in Chromium EC codebase.  I put comments of them so that it\u0027s easy to lookup the relevant STM32F072 documentation for what each of these lines is doing.\n\nI don\u0027t know why the official STM libraries are not used in the Chromium EC codebase, but my guess is their license may not be compatible with the Chromium open source license.  (That\u0027s a total guess, I haven\u0027t checked their licenses, and IANAL).\n\nLet me know if you want me to #define in this file just the macros I\u0027m using here.  I\u0027d rather not put an incomplete set in stm32/registers.h[1] or any common header, and I\u0027d also rather not hold this change up for manually-ish defining the entire set from documentation.  (I\u0027d try to script it from the PDF docs covering the actual registers, but it\u0027d still be a decent chunk of work to get the parsing right, I suspect.)\n\nIdeally we\u0027d just add at least the headers from STM\u0027s own libraries, but I\u0027d want buy-in from someone with much more experience and understanding of open source licensing than myself.\n\n\n[1] https://cs.corp.google.com/chromeos_public/src/platform/ec/chip/stm32/registers.h",
      "parentUuid": "e7a2dce3_c69a6b1d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 450,
        "startChar": 6,
        "endLine": 450,
        "endChar": 25
      },
      "revId": "bf3d7d392472c74198367681671c0330c5985697",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ebd6a587_556cfb7a",
        "filename": "board/servo_micro/board.c",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 450,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000104
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-08-02T23:10:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, adding these to registers.h would be good.",
      "parentUuid": "e34031cd_e51b5f0b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 450,
        "startChar": 6,
        "endLine": 450,
        "endChar": 25
      },
      "revId": "bf3d7d392472c74198367681671c0330c5985697",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0d384936_67eae911",
        "filename": "board/servo_micro/board.c",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 450,
      "author": {
        "id": 1129199
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-08-03T02:25:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Please do not copy anything from STM libraries (I think their licence is quite restrictive).",
      "parentUuid": "ebd6a587_556cfb7a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 450,
        "startChar": 6,
        "endLine": 450,
        "endChar": 25
      },
      "revId": "bf3d7d392472c74198367681671c0330c5985697",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a711a641_629dc8b8",
        "filename": "board/servo_micro/board.c",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 453,
      "author": {
        "id": 1129199
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-08-02T02:14:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think you can just disable the timers here, no need to reset all regs.",
      "revId": "bf3d7d392472c74198367681671c0330c5985697",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c08d62d4_036c0a4a",
        "filename": "board/servo_micro/board.c",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 453,
      "author": {
        "id": 1291807
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-08-02T22:07:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That is true, but it\u0027s no more code to just call reset_tim16_tim17() since it exists anyways.  I think it\u0027s polite to reset everything, e.g. if another routine using these timers isn\u0027t as defensive.",
      "parentUuid": "a711a641_629dc8b8",
      "revId": "bf3d7d392472c74198367681671c0330c5985697",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7a984223_2de516f3",
        "filename": "board/servo_micro/board.c",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 453,
      "author": {
        "id": 1129199
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-08-03T02:25:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Well, what I\u0027m saying is that you don\u0027t actually need either of the calls.\n\nNote that this is EC code where space is quite limited (do a makes savesizes before your change, and make newsizes after your change to get an idea), and we usually sacrifice defensiveness for code space.\n\nIf you define these timers somewhere in board.h (like we do for TIM_CLOCK32, for example), I don\u0027t think it\u0027s so likely we\u0027ll get confused.",
      "parentUuid": "c08d62d4_036c0a4a",
      "revId": "bf3d7d392472c74198367681671c0330c5985697",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    }
  ]
}